-- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5989+) **Recheck and reassign citizens to safe, clearly better unworked plots:** K-Mod could keep a weaker worked (i.e. assigned to one population in city) plot because its quick initial estimate overlooked another plot that its full city-aware comparison considered better. If ordinary citizen allocation finds no change, the **AI now rechecks plots that improve at least one yield without reducing any**, **trade some production for a large food/commerce gain**, or otherwise **offer a substantial overall gain without losing food**. It switches **only when** the full city-aware valuation confirms the change is **beneficial**, never when the swap would cause starvation, and does not immediately reverse a plot assigned earlier in the same update. The newly added `SAS_BBAI_CITIZEN_LOG_LEVEL` BBAI logging test showed this corrected cases such as Karakorum working **2 food / 0 hammers / 1 commerce** instead of the strictly better **2 food / 1 hammer / 1 commerce** plot, made 624 approved swaps through turn 359 at normal game speed, and reduced remaining plot-to-plot contextual misses from 4,187 to 3,229 (about 23%); specialist-related swaps remain a separate target. (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5990+) Note: for convenience, human cities use the same fallback by default (tunable) through `SAS_CONVENIENCE_HUMAN_CITIZEN_PLOT_FALLBACK_ENABLE`, but only while citizen automation is enabled; manual citizen assignments remain untouched.
-- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5995+) **Recheck modest food trades missed by K-Mod's quick plot estimate:** Additionally to the previous change, BBAI logging still found recurring high-value cases such as working **2 food / 1 hammer / 1 commerce** instead of **3 food / 0 hammers / 1 commerce**, or **3 food / 1 hammer / 1 commerce** instead of **4 food / 0 hammers / 1 commerce**. The fallback now also considers an unworked plot that provides at least **+1 food** while losing no more than **1 hammer and 2 commerce**, but reassigns the population only when the full city-aware comparison confirms that the trade is beneficial and the existing starvation/stability safeguards pass. Across directionally comparable but diverging map-428 BBAI runs through turn 348, this made 780 approved modest-food trades; unresolved records matching the new pattern fell from 1,460 to 0, all remaining plot-to-plot contextual-miss records fell from 3,702 to 2,404, and those valued above 1,000 fell from 762 to 162.
-- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5997+) **Consider additional beneficial food trades missed by K-Mod's quick plot estimate:** Additionally to the previous change, BBAI logging still found the preceding narrow limits could still exclude worthwhile changes such as **2 food / 0 hammers / 3 commerce** to **3 food / 0 hammers / 0 commerce**, even when the city's full valuation strongly preferred the extra food. The fallback now also checks any plot trade that gains at least **+1 food** without reducing the simple diagnostic score of **3 food + 2 hammers + 1 commerce**. This score only identifies candidates: the full city-aware comparison must still approve every reassignment, and the existing starvation and stability safeguards remain in force. In directionally comparable but diverging map-428 runs through turn 340, the new rule made 292 approved reassignments, eliminated all 372 previously unresolved records matching this pattern, reduced all remaining plot-to-plot misses from 2,434 to 1,936, and reduced those valued above 1,000 from 211 to 88; no new-rule reassignment was reversed within one turn.
